## Refactoring Complete

**Naming Evaluation (First Priority):**
- `nextGeneration`, `cellKey`, `survivesWithNeighborCount`, `isBornWithNeighborCount`, `neighborsOf`, `uniqueCells`, `isAlive`, `aliveNeighborCount`, `candidates` — all clearly reveal intent. No renames needed.
- Added a new well-named predicate `willBeAlive` capturing "will this cell be alive in the next generation" — a domain concept that was previously implicit in an inline ternary.

**Refactoring Applied — Extract `willBeAlive` predicate (Rule 2: Reveals Intent):**

Before:
```typescript
return candidates.filter((cell) => {
  const neighbors = aliveNeighborCount(cell);
  return isAlive(cell)
    ? survivesWithNeighborCount(neighbors)
    : isBornWithNeighborCount(neighbors);
});
```

After:
```typescript
const willBeAlive = (cell: Cell): boolean => {
  const count = aliveNeighborCount(cell);
  return isAlive(cell)
    ? survivesWithNeighborCount(count)
    : isBornWithNeighborCount(count);
};

const candidates = uniqueCells([...cells, ...cells.flatMap(neighborsOf)]);

return candidates.filter(willBeAlive);
```

**APP Mass Change:**
- Before (inline block): filter(2) + arrow(2) + binding neighbors(1) + aliveNeighborCount call(2) + ternary(4) + isAlive call(2) + survives call(2) + born call(2) = ~17
- After (extracted + filter call): willBeAlive binding(1) + arrow(2) + count binding(1) + aliveNeighborCount call(2) + ternary(4) + isAlive call(2) + survives call(2) + born call(2) + filter(2) + willBeAlive reference(1) = ~19

